{
  "description": "health.v2 §2.2, §2.4: a late joiner's reading of one owner's answer to a GET over zk2/lab/svc/health.v2/state/** (core §4.2, §7.5). Computed twice by two scripts of the text's drafter that share no code, kept out of the repository, and never blessed. `epoch` is the deployment epoch in seconds. `replies` are the GET's replies, each its `key` and its payload in `hex`: a snapshot's page, the status's on its own key with collection index 1 and one entry of the empty id, the checks' on .../state/checks with collection index 0 and one entry per check, its id the check's name. Every page is one core §7.5 accepts. `expect.status` and `expect.checks` are null where no page of that collection was read, else: `complete` (the reader holds a page of each index up to one whose more bit is 0), the snapshot's `run` (4 lowercase hexadecimal digits for a 16-bit run, 8 for a 32-bit run), its `asof` and its `time` in milliseconds since the Unix epoch. The status's `entry` is null (no entry), a tombstone ({tombstone: true, stamp}) or a live entry; the checks' `live` and `retired` list their live entries and tombstones in the order read, each with its `check`. A live entry is its `stamp` (<run>/<seq>, the entry's own run where it states one), its `confirmation` (`none`, `time`: vouched for at the snapshot's time, or `conf`: its last confirmation), `confirmed_at` in milliseconds since the Unix epoch (null for none) and its `record`, read by core §7.6 under the page's tag as records.json reads it: the fields, or {refused: token}. `expect.instant` is §2.2's one instant: both snapshots read and complete, under one run in width and value and one asof, and no live entry or tombstone of that run with a seq above the asof; an entry that states its own run breaks nothing. `expect.status_better_than_a_check` is null unless the reading is one instant and the status's record reads at a level; then it is true when a live check's record reads at a worse level, the break of §2.2 a tool may report from this reading alone, and false otherwise. A check at unknown, and one whose record is refused, bound nothing.",
